WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.672
Let's work out four fifths take away one fifth.

2
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.153
Here are four fifths.

3
00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:17.619
Take one fifth away.

4
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.897
Take away the tops. The bottom stays the same.

5
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:27.375
Now three quarters take away one third.

6
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:33.200
The bottoms are different. The parts don't match.

7
00:00:35.167 --> 00:00:37.628
The LCM of 4 and 3 is 12.

8
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.550
Cut both bars into 12 parts.

9
00:00:43.533 --> 00:00:45.530
Three quarters is 9 twelfths.

10
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:48.265
One third is 4 twelfths.

11
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:52.694
Start with 9 twelfths. Take 4 away.

12
00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.243
Nine minus four is five. The answer is five twelfths.

13
00:01:05.233 --> 00:01:08.112
Make the bottoms match, then take away the tops.
